<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manichaeism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Manichaean</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manichaeism was a religion founded by the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> in the third century CE, teaching a dualism of light and darkness. It spread widely from the Roman world to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> it was practised in China, notably among Sogdian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> communities, before being suppressed in the ninth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manichaeism.jpg" alt="Manichaeism" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manicheans.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
